course: dictionary
lesson: 15844
title: Undistributed: not yet shared out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Look at the parts of the word. Un- means not, distribute means to share out or give out, and -ed shows that it describes something. So undistributed means not yet shared out or given out. «Fourteen books were still undistributed, so they stayed in the box.» The books were waiting to be handed out.
explain: Use the context to check. Ask: is the thing being handed out to people, or is it still waiting? If it is still waiting, it is undistributed. Try the swap: «Fourteen books were still waiting to be shared out, so they stayed in the box.» The meaning still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: In business and logic, the word has special meanings. «The company kept its profits undistributed» means it did not pay the money to its owners. The words about money and owners are the clues. Always read the words around a hard word first.
fact: Un- means not, and distribute means to share out or give out.
fact: «Undistributed» means not shared out or given out yet.
fact: In business, «undistributed profits» are profits a company keeps instead of paying them to its owners.
fact: In logic, the «undistributed middle» is a mistake in reasoning, when a term does not cover all of its group.
fact: A good check is to swap in "still waiting to be shared out": if it fits, the meaning is right.
exercise: «Fourteen books were still undistributed, so they stayed in the box.» What does undistributed mean? | Very heavy | Shared out to everyone | *Not yet shared out | Broken and thrown away
exercise: «The food was undistributed because the lorries were stuck in the snow.» Why was the food undistributed? | Everyone had already eaten it | It was too hot to eat | The food was very tasty | *The lorries were stuck in the snow
exercise: «The company kept its profits undistributed, so the owners got no money.» What does undistributed mean here? | Spent on new lorries | *Not paid out to the owners | Paid out to the owners in full | Lost in the post
test: «The aid parcels stayed undistributed in the warehouse for three weeks.» What does undistributed mean? | Stolen by thieves | *Not yet given out to the people who need them | Given out to everyone at once | Very cold
test: Mia asks why the sweets are still in the bag. Which answer uses undistributed correctly? | *The sweets are still undistributed, because nobody has handed them out yet | The sweets are undistributed because they are sour | The sweets are undistributed because the bag is red | The sweets are undistributed because they have all been eaten
exam: In logic, what is «the undistributed middle»? | *A mistake in reasoning where a term does not cover all of its group | A very long sentence | A correct and fair argument | A middle part of a story that is missing
